  "_doc": [
    "Published retail values for types 0..14 as on Sega's US servers after the Illuminus update (2008..2009, type level cap 20). Types 10..15 are placeholder rows on the AotI disc (every % 100); its rows for 0..9 are the offline-mode values.",
    "Applied by: python gamedata.py --game aoti --type-overrides aoti_type_overrides.json [--type-fill linear|disc].",
    "Facts transcribed from fan wikis (PSUPedia, US Network mode; archive.org snapshots), not Sega data; every source is in the type's sources and in work/retail-types-sources.md.",
    "levels: type level -> [HP, ATP, ATA, TP, DFP, EVP, MST, STA] % in PSUPedia's column order; null = not published (--type-fill linear interpolates, --type-fill disc keeps the disc value).",
    "estimated: type level -> columns PSUPedia printed in parentheses (its own estimates). inferred: values that are not printed anywhere but follow from the sources (each type's sources say how).",
    "race_pct: per-race bonus (PSUPedia 'Favored Types'); omitted races are 100 (the discs' 95 % penalties are offline-only).",
    "requirements: type -> minimum type level, replaces the disc row. cap: retail type level cap (type_caps in plylevel.json); stat_cap: last level with stat gains (rows above hold it; default cap).",
    "exp_curve: name in exp_curves = cumulative type EXP (MP) at type level 1, 2, ...; null = not published (interpolated); levels past the cap continue the last step.",
    "The hidden S5 % (row index 7) is not published anywhere and stays as on the disc.",
    "Acromaster is absent: it was never released on Sega's servers (Clementine added its own), so its disc row, requirements and type EXP stay."
